      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I will just respond with that the keyboard is part of the UI.\nThey redesign the UI now with some new fancy transitions and better control over the UI (not just a redesign). The keyboard functionality is still part of it, they also added a option to disable snapping on sliders.\nFurther off-topic (not meant to get a response, this just to make a point)\nI prefer to see it in the same update instead of having half updates all the time.\nPhysics Bones & interactions was also announced for worlds so people could directly interact with the world (still not here)\nWith the new UI was promised that worlds get there own tab (probably won't be in this update)\nWith OSC was promised that world where able to store data on the servers so you could have settings, scores etc across the same world when you would switch. (Also still not here)\nThe point that I am trying to have is, that half updates just don't make sense.\nBUT I do understand that in the current situation people want features (QUICK) and not having to wait for half a year.\nBut something like a keyboard is a small & quick fix. \nIts probably like a small fixed threshold value when a trigger should be registered as a 'new' click/interaction\n^\nI don't know the structure of VRChats code but as a developer myself this shouldn't be a big thing to fix. This might be just a 10m change/fix. As I said before, I don't know the structure.\nThe person that official wrote it or the person that knows the most about it should be able to change this pretty quick. Most work will be in what will be the 'best' threshold. (ofc can be more complicated based on what controllers people use etc)",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
